Package: neo-settings
Architecture: any
Depends: python3,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-glib-2.0,
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: accountsservice,
            network-manager,
            gnome-keyring,
            pkexec,
Description: settings app for GNOME Phone
 Neo Settings is One UI's Settings for GNOME Phone: connections (Wi-Fi,
 Bluetooth, mobile network, hotspot), sounds, notifications, display, battery,
 wallpaper and parallax sets, the home screen's icon pack and shapes, the lock
 screen (PIN, pattern, password), location, accounts, apps, language, date and
 time, accessibility and the phone's details. GNOME Phone opens it wherever
 GNOME opens a Settings panel.

Package: neo-weather
Architecture: any
Depends: curl,
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: geoclue-2.0,
Description: weather app for GNOME Phone
 Neo Weather shows the weather where the phone is: the next 24 hours, today
 against yesterday, the week and the details. The forecast is Open-Meteo's,
 the place a city chosen in the app (a search by name, which works with
 Location off), else GNOME Weather's first city, else GeoClue's, named by
 OpenStreetMap's Nominatim.

Package: neo-camera
Architecture: any
Depends: gstreamer1.0-libcamera,
         gstreamer1.0-plugins-base,
         gstreamer1.0-plugins-good,
         gstreamer1.0-gtk4,
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad,
            gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly,
            gstreamer1.0-libav,
            gstreamer1.0-pulseaudio,
Description: camera app for GNOME Phone
 Neo Camera is LineageOS's Aperture rebuilt in GTK 4 on libcamera and
 GStreamer: photos (JPEG with EXIF in ~/Pictures/Camera), videos (H.264 and
 AAC in ~/Videos/Camera) and barcode scanning, with the front and rear
 cameras, flash, timer, grid and level. It runs on any phone libcamera
 supports; the video encoder is the fastest one that works (V4L2, VA-API,
 openh264 or x264).

Package: neo-files
