         ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: gvfs-backends,
            gvfs-fuse,
            xdg-desktop-portal-gnome,
Description: file manager for GNOME Phone
 Neo Files is File Manager+ rebuilt in GTK 4 on GIO and GVfs: the phone's
 storage, removable media, the recycle bin, recent files, the local network
 and saved remotes over SMB, SFTP, FTP/FTPS and WebDAV.

Package: neo-iconpack-round
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: neo-launcher,
Description: Round icon pack for the Neo launcher
 Round, colourful icons for GNOME Phone's apps and the GNOME apps it keeps:
 a white Material Symbols glyph on a gradient disc in each app's colour.
 Installing it makes it the launcher's icon pack; Neo Settings' Home screen
 switches packs.

Package: neo-icon-themes
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         adwaita-icon-theme,
         hicolor-icon-theme,
Description: GNOME Phone's icon packs as icon themes
 The Renaissance (night, day; glyph night, glyph day) and Round icon packs
 as freedesktop icon themes (neo-renaissance-night, neo-round, ...): the
 stock setting org.gnome.desktop.interface icon-theme, or Neo Settings'
 Appearance page, selects one, and the shell's app grid and every GTK
 program use it. Names a theme lacks come from Adwaita and hicolor.

Package: neo-parallax-solar-system
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: neo-launcher,
Description: NASA solar-system parallax wallpaper for the Neo launcher
 A layered wallpaper that moves with the phone's tilt on GNOME Phone's Neo
 launcher: the Sun, Earth, the Moon, Mars, Saturn and Jupiter from NASA's
 public-domain images over a drawn star field. Installing it makes it the
 default wallpaper; GNOME Settings' Background panel lists it too.

Package: neo-remote
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Recommends: minerva-ir,
Description: infrared remote app for GNOME Phone
 Neo Remote turns a phone with an IR LED into a remote for the TV and any
 other device: remotes found by brand (each Power code of the brand tried in
 turn until the device reacts) or by model in the code database, a grid of
 buttons per remote, buttons of your own, and macros recorded by tapping.
 Everything infrared is Minerva's minerva-ir service (org.minerva.Ir1).
